CATEGORIES:Podcast - TWiV
DESCRIPTION:[Podcast: This Week in Virology]\n\nIn his weekly clinical upd
 ate\, Daniel Griffin and Vincent Racaniello are distressed by Erica Schwar
 tz’ confirmation as CDC director\, the GAO proposed pandemic preparednes
 s plans\, the national cyclospora outbreak and resulting two deaths\, new 
 screwworm and the scale of the Ebola outbreak in the Congo\, and clear res
 ults from some of President Trump’s policies dismantling public health a
 ctivites including water safety\, before Dr. Griffin deep dives into the m
 easles outbreak\, recent statistics on RSV\, influenza and SARS-CoV-2 infe
 ctions\, the Wasterwater Scan dashboard\, Johns Hopkins measles tracker\, 
 FDA approval of Moderna’s mRNA vaccine for seasonal flu\, how to access 
 and pay for Paxlovid\, where to go for answers about long COVID-19\, how S
 ARS-CoV-2 infections may reactivate latent viral infections\, particularly
  Aniello virus\, and contacting your federal government representative to 
 stop the assault on science and biomedical research. Click arrow to play D
 ownload&nbsp\; TWiV 1346 (33 MB .mp3\, 54 min) Subscribe (free):&nbsp\; Ap
 ple Podcasts \, RSS \,&nbsp\; email Become a&nbsp\; patron &nbsp\;of&nbsp
 \;TWiV! Links for this episode Senate confirms Erica Schwartz as CDC direc
 tor (CIDRAP) 2:10 PUBLIC HEALTH PREPAREDNESS: Experts Identified Actions t
 o Improve Surveillance for Emerging Disease Threats (Government Accountabi
 lity Office) 4:10 Association Between First MMR Vaccination Before Age 2 Y
 ears and Childhood Autism in a U.S. EHR Cohort of 2.5 Million Children (Th
 e Pediatric Infectious Dis\n\nEvent URL: https://www.microbe.tv/twiv/twiv-
 1346/\n\nSource: twiv_podcast
LOCATION:Podcast
URL:https://www.microbe.tv/twiv/twiv-1346/
