BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Science-Based Strategies to Support Your Immune System
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260922T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260922T200000
DTSTAMP:20260905T061305Z
UID:198f8cc9a8b9603c@gid-seminars.wnprc.wisc.edu
CATEGORIES:Class/Seminar
DESCRIPTION:The immune system is a remarkably complex network of organs\, 
 cells\, and chemical messengers that protects us from infection every day.
  Yet we're constantly bombarded with products\, remedies\, and online advi
 ce claiming to "boost" immunity. How can you tell what's supported by scie
 nce and what's simply marketing?\n\nIn this noontime webinar\, you'll lear
 n how the immune system works\, how it changes as we age\, and what lifest
 yle habits truly support immune health. We'll separate fact from fiction a
 s we examine the evidence behind nutrition\, exercise\, sleep\, stress man
 agement\, supplements\, and other popular immune remedies.\n\nYou'll also 
 discover why vaccines work differently from remedies that claim to "boost"
  immunity\, how they train the immune system to recognize specific threats
 \, and why vaccination remains one of the most effective tools for prevent
 ing serious infectious diseases.\n\nYou'll leave with practical\, evidence
 -based strategies you can use right away and a clearer understanding of wh
 at really supports a healthy immune system.\n\nThis class will be recorded
  and a one-week link to the recording will be shared with all registered p
 articipants. \n\nTo receive incentive points\, attend at least 80% of the 
 live session or listen to the entire recording within one week.  \n\nReque
 st disability accommodations and access info.\n\nClass details are subject
  to change.\n\nEvent URL: https://events.stanford.edu/event/science-based-
 strategies-to-support-your-immune-system\n\nSource: stanford_virtual
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/science-based-strategies-to-support-
 your-immune-system
